b.com/users/gkalpak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-07-10T09:21:15Z","updated_at":"2017-07-10T09:21:15Z","body":"This is actually not an issue with animations (or mdTabs), but with angular.io.\r\n\r\nIt happens because of [this line][1], which is supposed (based on the comment) to just remove the ripple effect (no idea why 😞), but is sure does more than that :smiley:\r\nWhile animating, mdTab will set a `transform` style on the tab content element, which should have no effect (due to our `transform: none !important` style afaict), so Firefox seems to do the right thing. For some reason, Chrome doesn't respect the `!important` part and executes the animation anyway.\r\n\r\n[1]: https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/cc611c93b6748717f660bc99124bb4f8b9bc0fa3/aio/src/styles/2-modules/_code.scss#L116-L118","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/314052417/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"gkalpak","id":8604205,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2MDQyMDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8604205?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak","html_url":"https://github.com/gkalpak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github